.TH FL-SERVICES 1 "November 2026" "fldesktop 0.1.4" "fldesktop"
.SH NAME
fl-services \- start, stop, enable and disable system services
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBfl-services\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
Lists the system's services with their state (running, stopped, failed)
and whether they start at boot, from systemd or OpenRC. Start, Stop and
Restart act now; Enable and Disable decide about the boot (with systemd
they also start or stop the service). The status of the selected service is
shown below the list. With systemd your user services are listed too.
.PP
Changing system services needs an administrator: systemd asks through
polkit; with OpenRC \fBfl-services-helper\fR runs through \fBpkexec\fR(1).
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBsystemctl\fR(1), \fBrc-service\fR(8), \fBrc-update\fR(8), \fBfl-logs\fR(1)
